    {
      "id": "TIMPF3UW",
      "key": "TIMPF3UW",
      "version": 0,
      "html": "<div data-citation-items=\"%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FZES5ADPW%22%5D%2C%22itemData%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19922179%2Fitems%2FZES5ADPW%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22article%22%2C%22abstract%22%3A%22Despite%20transformative%20advances%20in%20generative%20motion%20synthesis%2C%20real-time%20interactive%20motion%20control%20remains%20dominated%20by%20traditional%20techniques.%20In%20this%20work%2C%20we%20identify%20two%20key%20challenges%20in%20bridging%20research%20and%20production%3A%201)%20Real-time%20scalability%3A%20Industry%20applications%20demand%20real-time%20generation%20of%20a%20vast%20repertoire%20of%20motion%20skills%2C%20while%20generative%20methods%20exhibit%20significant%20degradation%20in%20quality%20and%20scalability%20under%20real-time%20computation%20constraints%2C%20and%202)%20Integration%3A%20Industry%20applications%20demand%20fine-grained%20multi-modal%20control%20involving%20velocity%20commands%2C%20style%20selection%2C%20and%20precise%20keyframes%2C%20a%20need%20largely%20unmet%20by%20existing%20text-%20or%20tag-driven%20models.%20To%20overcome%20these%20limitations%2C%20we%20introduce%20MotionBricks%3A%20a%20large-scale%2C%20real-time%20generative%20framework%20with%20a%20two-fold%20solution.%20First%2C%20we%20propose%20a%20large-scale%20modular%20latent%20generative%20backbone%20tailored%20for%20robust%20real-time%20motion%20generation%2C%20effectively%20modeling%20a%20dataset%20of%20over%20350%2C000%20motion%20clips%20with%20a%20single%20model.%20Second%2C%20we%20introduce%20smart%20primitives%20that%20provide%20a%20unified%2C%20robust%2C%20and%20intuitive%20interface%20for%20authoring%20both%20navigation%20and%20object%20interaction.%20Applications%20can%20be%20designed%20in%20a%20plug-and-play%20manner%20like%20assembling%20bricks%20without%20expert%20animation%20knowledge.%20Quantitatively%2C%20we%20show%20that%20MotionBricks%20produces%20state-of-the-art%20motion%20quality%20on%20open-source%20and%20proprietary%20datasets%20of%20various%20scales%2C%20while%20also%20achieving%20a%20real-time%20throughput%20of%2015%2C000%20FPS%20with%202ms%20latency.%20We%20demonstrate%20the%20flexibility%20and%20robustness%20of%20MotionBricks%20in%20a%20complete%20production-level%20animation%20demo%2C%20covering%20navigation%20and%20object-scene%20interaction%20across%20various%20styles%20with%20a%20unified%20model.%20To%20showcase%20our%20framework's%20application%20beyond%20animation%2C%20we%20deploy%20MotionBricks%20on%20the%20Unitree%20G1%20humanoid%20robot%20to%20demonstrate%20its%20flexibility%20and%20generalization%20for%20real-time%20robotic%20control.%22%2C%22DOI%22%3A%2210.48550%2FarXiv.2604.24833%22%2C%22language%22%3A%22en%22%2C%22note%22%3A%22arXiv%3A2604.24833%20%5Bcs.RO%5D%22%2C%22number%22%3A%22arXiv%3A2604.24833%22%2C%22publisher%22%3A%22arXiv%22%2C%22source%22%3A%22arXiv.org%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22MotionBricks%3A%20Scalable%20Real-Time%20Motions%20with%20Modular%20Latent%20Generative%20Model%20and%20Smart%20Primitives%22%2C%22title-short%22%3A%22MotionBricks%22%2C%22URL%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fabs%2F2604.24833%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Wang%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Tingwu%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Dionne%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Olivier%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Ruyter%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Michael%20De%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Minor%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22David%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Rempe%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Davis%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Zhao%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Kaifeng%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Petrovich%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Mathis%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Yuan%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Ye%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Li%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Chenran%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Luo%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Zhengyi%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Robison%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Brian%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Blackwell%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Xavier%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Antoniazzi%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Bernardo%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Peng%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Xue%20Bin%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Zhu%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Yuke%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Yuen%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Simon%22%7D%5D%2C%22accessed%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%2C6%2C10%5D%5D%7D%2C%22issued%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%2C4%2C27%5D%5D%7D%7D%7D%5D\" data-schema-version=\"9\"><p>Comment: ACM Transactions on Graphics; SIGGRAPH 2026. Project page: https://nvlabs.github.io/motionbricks/</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>MotionBricks : large-scale, real-time generative framework with a two-fold solution</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"1354\" height=\"770\" data-attachment-key=\"NKIBYVHC\"></p>\n<p>Multi-head Tokenizer:</p>\n<p>Root module: predicts timing and initial root trajectories</p>\n<p>Pose module: model encoded pose token distributions conditioned on the in-betweening constraints and root predictions</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Flexible in-betweening formulation:<br><img alt=\"\" width=\"661\" height=\"367\" data-attachment-key=\"9QWMNMVS\"></p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"667\" height=\"622\" data-attachment-key=\"D5PJT7XY\"></p>\n<p>Structured Multi-headed Tokenizer</p>\n<p>Representation</p>\n<p>(rg, rl, p, q, v, c), comprising: </p>\n<p>(1) global root values rg: projected global positions and the cosine and sine of the heading angle of the pelvis joint; </p>\n<p>(2) local root values rl : projected positional velocity and angular velocity of the pelvis joint in global coordinates; </p>\n<p>(3) joint positions p and rotations q for all joints (excluding the projected root joint);</p>\n<p>(4) joint velocities v and contact labels c.</p>\n<p>1.Encoder<img alt=\"\" width=\"642\" height=\"243\" data-attachment-key=\"WDD47484\"></p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"665\" height=\"233\" data-attachment-key=\"QZ4B6XDT\"></p>\n<p>2.Decoder</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"659\" height=\"267\" data-attachment-key=\"5QGPA5CM\"></p>\n<p>3. Quantizer and Training</p>\n<p>VQ-VAE loss</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"492\" height=\"36\" data-attachment-key=\"HY5M3SM3\"></p>\n<p></p>\n<p>Neural Backbone - progressive modular architecture (coarse-to-fine)</p>\n<p>1.root module</p>\n<p>step 1. Hidden state initialization and timing prediction</p>\n<p>Transformer Encoder (16 learnable frame-shot + global embedding for keyframe constraints + timing embedding)</p>\n<p>step 2. Conditional root trajectory estimation</p>\n<p>mask out the ones beyond predicted frame count, temporal transformer</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"564\" height=\"149\" data-attachment-key=\"XKRBNDFL\"></p>\n<p>2.pose module - (1) local and global root values rl, rg (2) local pose keyframe constraints p,q (3) pose token embeddings</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"595\" height=\"390\" data-attachment-key=\"G3FUUQAV\"></p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"723\" height=\"916\" data-attachment-key=\"J37UJ3TC\"></p>\n<p>Smart Primitives - Generalization by Scalable Neural Backbone</p>\n<p>1.smart locomotion </p>\n<p>Critically Damped Spring Model for Initial Root Trajectory Estimation<br><img alt=\"\" width=\"636\" height=\"238\" data-attachment-key=\"ZVI7VPTT\"></p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"1327\" height=\"740\" data-attachment-key=\"88LSSJWV\"></p>\n<p>Style Control via Keyframe Selection - powerful generative backbone + replanning mechanism</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"654\" height=\"243\" data-attachment-key=\"373V549Y\"></p>\n<p>Neural Refinement - ↑</p>\n<p><img alt=\"\" width=\"1279\" height=\"1034\" data-attachment-key=\"TI2IXYGE\"></p>\n<p>2.smart object</p>\n<p>Intent keyframes: define the essential poses for an interaction behavior - Drop-frame attribute</p>\n<p>Interaction Binding: detection, object sockets and placement, keyframe anchoring</p>\n<p></p>\n</div>",
